### ============================================================
### COMPLETE END-TO-END WORKFLOW VIA GATEWAY
### ============================================================

### Step 1: Register Customer Account
POST {{gateway}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "e2e_customer",
  "email": "e2e@smartship.com",
  "password": "E2E@123"
}

###

### Step 2: Login to Get Token
POST {{gateway}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "e2e_customer",
  "password": "E2E@123"
}

###

### Step 3: Create Shipment (extract shipment_id from response)
POST {{gateway}}/shipments
Authorization: Bearer {{customer_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderName": "E2E Sender",
  "senderAddress": "100 Main St, NYC, NY 10001",
  "senderPhone": "+1-555-1111",
  "recipientName": "E2E Recipient",
  "recipientAddress": "200 Park Ave, LA, CA 90001",
  "recipientPhone": "+1-555-2222",
  "itemDescription": "E2E Test Package",
  "weight": 1.5,
  "dimensions": "25x15x10 cm",
  "estimatedValue": 100.00,
  "serviceType": "STANDARD"
}

###

### Step 4: Book Shipment (transitions Draft → Booked)
PUT {{gateway}}/shipments/{{sample_shipment_id}}/book
Authorization: Bearer {{customer_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Step 5: Get Tracking Timeline
GET {{gateway}}/tracking/{{sample_shipment_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Step 6: Update Status - Picked Up
PUT {{gateway}}/tracking/{{sample_shipment_id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{customer_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PICKED_UP",
  "location": "NYC Pickup Center"
}

###

### Step 7: Update Status - In Transit
PUT {{gateway}}/tracking/{{sample_shipment_id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{customer_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "IN_TRANSIT",
  "location": "Regional Hub - Chicago"
}

###

### Step 8: Update Status - Out for Delivery
PUT {{gateway}}/tracking/{{sample_shipment_id}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{customer_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "OUT_FOR_DELIVERY",
  "location": "Local Delivery Station - LA"
}

###

### Step 9: Submit Delivery Proof
POST {{gateway}}/tracking/{{sample_shipment_id}}/delivery-proof
Authorization: Bearer {{customer_token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="recipientName"

E2E Recipient
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="deliveryLocation"

200 Park Ave, LA, CA 90001
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--

###

### Step 10: Verify Final Tracking Status
GET {{gateway}}/tracking/{{sample_shipment_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### ============================================================
### INFORMATION & NOTES
### ============================================================

# GATEWAY ROUTING CONFIGURATION:
# The Gateway routes requests to microservices based on URL prefix:
#
# /auth/*       → Auth Service (http://localhost:5045/api/auth/*)
# /admin/*      → Admin Service (http://localhost:5127/api/admin/*)
# /shipments/*  → Shipment Service (http://localhost:5286/api/shipments/*)
# /tracking/*   → Tracking Service (http://localhost:5062/api/tracking/*)

# AUTHENTICATION:
# - /auth/signup and /auth/login are PUBLIC (no token required)
# - ALL other endpoints (including /tracking/*) require Bearer token via Gateway
# - Note: Individual tracking service may not require auth, but Gateway enforces it
# - Extract token from login response and save to @auth_token or @customer_token
# - Use: Authorization: Bearer {{customer_token}} for all protected routes

# USER ROLES:
# - CUSTOMER: Can create/manage own shipments, view tracking
# - ADMIN: Full access to all admin endpoints and monitoring

# SHIPMENT STATUS TRANSITIONS:
# DRAFT → BOOKED → PICKED_UP → IN_TRANSIT → OUT_FOR_DELIVERY → DELIVERED
# OR
# DRAFT/BOOKED → CANCELLED (if canceled before pickup)

# HTTP STATUS CODES:
# 200 - OK (successful request)
# 201 - Created (resource created)
# 400 - Bad Request (validation error)
# 401 - Unauthorized (missing/invalid token)
# 403 - Forbidden (insufficient permissions)
# 404 - Not Found (resource doesn't exist)
# 500 - Internal Server Error

# TESTING TIPS:
# 1. Use Step 1-2 to get valid tokens first
# 2. Update @customer_token and @admin_token with actual tokens
# 3. Copy shipment ID from Step 3 response into @sample_shipment_id
# 4. Use Variables section at top for all dynamic values
# 5. Test each section independently or run full workflow
